&lt;p&gt;At Mercury, building our customer base has been a wild and exciting adventure—and we’re just getting started. As we continue to grow, we’re looking for a thoughtful, driven Account Executive to help more founders and business owners discover and thrive with Mercury.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the past two years, we&#39;ve significantly expanded our startup customer base and we’re continuing on that journey to support even more startups and teams on Mercury. In this role you’ll have the opportunity to work closely with founders and finance leaders helping them shape the future of their finance stack with Mercury at the center. You’ll uncover pain points tied to current operations, run point on complex evaluations with multiple-products, and simplify the migration process across their full-stack into Mercury.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive, you’ll work directly with founders, business owners, and finance teams to deeply understand their operational needs and guide them to the right financial tools. You’ll immerse yourself in their ecosystems and uncover pain points to help them build great businesses with Mercury.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Here are some things you&#39;ll do on the job:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end sales process—from initial outreach to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our robust SDR team to build and nurture a strong outbound pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify new lead sources and learn about potential customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert signups into enthusiastic, long-term Mercury champions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a high volume of high-velocity sales cycles using internal tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our Relationship Management team to onboard complex customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with the Partnerships team to unlock new acquisition channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer feedback into insights that inform product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in San Francisco or New York City&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year of closing experience in a sales or account executive role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in building and managing a high-quality pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong discovery and consultative selling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A sense of urgency and ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to share feedback to improve our sales process and product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset and desire to support your teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills—able to simplify complex topics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and enthusiasm for helping innovative businesses grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for fintech and the future of financial tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mercury values diversity &amp;amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Mercury are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities or special needs. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;#LI-TG1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The total rewards package at Mercury includes base salary, equity (stock options/RSUs), and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary and equity ranges are highly competitive within the SaaS and fintech industry and are updated regularly using the most reliable compensation survey data for our industry. New hire offers are made based on a candidate’s experience, expertise, geographic location, and internal pay equity relative to peers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our target new hire base salary ranges for this role are the following&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US employees in New York City, Los Angeles, Seattle, or the San Francisco Bay Area:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$134,600&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$168,200 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US employees outside of New York City, Los Angeles, Seattle, or the San Francisco Bay Area:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$121,100&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$151,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mercury is building a complete finance stack for startups. We work hard to create the easiest and safest banking* experience possible to simplify entrepreneurs&#39; and business owners’ financial lives.The challenge is to do so while ensuring we protect Mercury, customers and the broader financial ecosystem from bad actors and harmful, illegal or unauthorized activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AML Investigations team is crucial in this mission and is responsible for detecting suspicious activity, conducting thorough investigations, and shutting down bad actors. This team is growing and we’re looking to hire an additional AML Risk Investigator to help us with Bank Partner Requests for Information, Transaction Monitoring, Financial Crime Investigations, Case Management and drafting Unusual Activity Reports. As a member of our Investigations team, you’ll help handle our transaction monitoring queues while balancing an eagle eye for risk with excellent user experience. To begin with, you’ll work to help make sure we have smart, risk-based monitoring in place and help build out our case management technology and processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll need to learn how a really wide range of businesses work and bring your knowledge to bear on our processes and product. Some of this work is repetitive and requires close attention to detail, so we need someone who loves working fraud and anti-money laundering transaction queues and managing a variety of complex investigations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;*&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As part of the journey, we would expect you to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input as we implement new transaction monitoring rules and tune existing ones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review AML, and other financial crime alerts in our transaction monitoring queue and take action as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contact our users for information on their account usage and transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our partners and internal team members to review and assess information received from users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and respond to Requests for Information (RFIs) from our Partner Banks, delivering clear, well-supported AML reviews on customer’s account activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decision user accounts as needed, including locking or closing accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an understanding of expected activity for each type of user we work with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document investigative findings and escalate unusual or potentially suspicious activity to our Partners for SAR consideration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop an unfailing eye for potential fraud or money laundering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate tools that would make your job easier&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clear documentation on current processes and help train future teammates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some things that might make you successful in a role like this:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience in identifying money laundering, detecting fraud, or other financial crimes related behavior in banking, fintech, or other financial services through vendor AND in-house developed transaction monitoring rules&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be fluent in the language of bank transactions, including ACH, check, debit card, credit card, and wire transfers, both domestic and international&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the business banking landscape and have familiarity with international activity and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise empathy and understanding when communicating with users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate complicated concepts with efficiency and clarity, both in speech and writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with external parties with confidence and kindness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with efficiency and focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand how to keep an organized and clean inbox&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love problem solving and making teams, product, and processes more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derive joy from customer joy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy thinking about how to automate as much of your job as possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be curious about the US banking system, startups, and ecommerce companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mercury values diversity &amp;amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Mercury are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities or special needs. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-DNI&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The total rewards package at Mercury includes base salary, equity (stock options/RSUs), and benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary and equity ranges are highly competitive within the SaaS and fintech industry and are updated regularly using the most reliable compensation survey data for our industry. New hire offers are made based on a candidate’s experience, expertise, geographic location, and internal pay equity relative to peers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our target new hire base salary ranges for this role are the following&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US employees in New York City, Los Angeles, Seattle, or the San Francisco Bay Area:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$121,700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$152,100 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;US employees outside of New York City, Los Angeles, Seattle, or the San Francisco Bay Area:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$109,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,900 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mercury is seeking a Business Continuity Management (BCM) Lead to build and lead an enterprise-wide continuity program as we prepare to become a bank. As part of the Risk team, this leader will establish practical standards, clear accountability, and tested capabilities to maintain critical services and recover effectively from disruptions, with direct visibility to the CRO and senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role fills the need for a dedicated leader to coordinate BCM across the organization. The ideal candidate combines deep continuity and resilience expertise with the judgment to build a proportionate program in a fast-moving environment, working effectively with Engineering, Operations, Product, Information Security, Legal, Compliance, and business teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The BCM Lead will own the enterprise framework, coordination, oversight, and reporting. Business and technology owners will remain accountable for their continuity plans and recovery execution.Because this is a new program, the Lead will be hands-on in the initial build: facilitating the first round of BIAs and plans side by side with owners, running exercises, and driving identified gaps through remediation. This leader will also work closely with Engineering on technology disaster recovery and with relevant teams on incident response, crisis management, and third-party resilience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement Mercury’s enterprise BCM framework, policies, standards, governance, and operating model, with a prioritized implementation roadmap aligned to bank-launch readiness and critical services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business owners to identify critical services, conduct business impact analyses (customer, financial, operational, and regulatory), and map dependencies across people, processes, technology, facilities, and third parties, including single points of failure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish recovery time objectives (RTOs) and recovery point objectives (RPOs), where applicable, with business and technology owners; challenge gaps between objectives and recovery capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set standards for continuity plans and recovery procedures, and facilitate and support accountable owners in developing actionable plans and alternative operating arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate business continuity with technology disaster recovery, incident response, and crisis management, with clear activation criteria, escalation paths, and communications responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and lead a risk-based exercise program, from tabletop simulations to end-to-end recovery tests, and drive lessons learned, remediation tracking, and verification that gaps are closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Third-Party Risk Management and vendor owners to assess critical provider recovery capabilities, contingency arrangements, and concentration dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed continuity considerations into new products, material business changes, and technology implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish metrics and reporting that give management and relevant committees visibility into readiness, testing outcomes, material gaps, and overdue remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a growing BCM team, including hiring and developing analysts as the program scales over the next year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver role-based training and promote awareness of continuity responsibilities across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory examinations and bank-launch readiness reviews with accurate documentation and evidence of recovery capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in business continuity management, operational resilience, disaster recovery, or a related discipline within a fintech, financial institution, technology company, or other highly regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building or materially enhancing an enterprise BCM program, including governance, implementation, testing, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in business impact analysis, critical-service identification, dependency mapping, and recovery objective development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing actionable continuity plans and leading exercises that test recovery assumptions and expose gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sufficient technical fluency to work with Engineering on cloud services, system dependencies, data recovery, and technology disaster recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of third-party risk management, including assessing critical vendor recovery capabilities, contingency arrangements and concentration risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to drive cross-functional remediation through influence, with a clear view of where BCM oversight ends and business or technology ownership begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain readiness gaps and tradeoffs to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team of Business Continuity analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with banking supervisory expectations for business continuity, and operational resilience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a company-building or bank-building environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with recognized continuity standards, such as ISO 22301, and BCM tools for plan management, exercises, and issue tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant professional certification, such as CBCP or MBCI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic, first-principles builder who turns ambiguous needs into clear priorities and designs a program that fits Mercury’s operations and scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takes ownership and follows through from identified gaps to demonstrated recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, low-ego, and effective across the three lines of defense.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm under pressure and able to facilitate clear decisions during disruptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to challenge constructively, distinguish material gaps from theoretical concerns, and avoid over-engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*Mercury is a fintech company, not an FDIC-insured bank. Banking services provided through Choice Financial Group and Column N.A., Members FDIC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mercury values diversity &amp;amp; belonging and is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer. All individuals seeking employment at Mercury are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, sexual orientation, or any other legally protected characteristic. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations throughout the recruitment process for applicants with disabilities or special needs. If you need assistance, or an accommodation, please let your recruiter know once you are contacted about a role.&lt;/p&gt;
