&lt;li&gt;Run kickoffs and calibration sessions with hiring managers to define what a strong candidate looks like, and adjust the search as you learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and engage strong candidates through sourcing and inbound channels, using funnel data to decide where to spend your time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and consistently with stakeholders on pipeline health, progress, blockers, and recruiting timeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Mercury to candidates, sharing our mission, culture, and what it&#39;s like to join a growing sales organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot opportunities to improve recruiting processes, tools, and documentation, and share them with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage offers and closing for your searches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll need&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, including at least 1 year in-house, ideally with sales roles such as account executives, SDRs, or account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and attention to detail, with experience managing several searches at once, including at least one high-volume role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sourcing skills and ability to write compelling outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with recruiting data, such as pass-through rates and time to hire, to track your searches and spot where they&#39;re getting stuck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building strong relationships with hiring managers, including giving clear feedback and pushing back when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently managing searches end to end, and knowing when to ask for help&lt;/li&gt;
