&lt;p&gt;At Mercury, research is a democratized practice. Designers and PMs talk directly to customers, and Research Operations builds and runs the system that makes that fast, high quality, and ethical. We&#39;re looking for a Research Operations Lead to build and run that program as Mercury scales. You&#39;ve done this before and have a clear point of view on how it should work. This is a hands-on leadership role: you’ll set the strategy and priorities for research enablement, develop the team, and personally lead work where senior judgment matters most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy, roadmap, and operating model for research at Mercury, enabling Product, Design, and Marketing to run research with autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply senior research judgment to complex or high-stakes work, using recurring gaps to strengthen the standards and guidance that raise research quality across Mercury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with design managers, designers, and PMs so customer evidence informs decisions from early discovery through post-launch usability and funnel analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our research tool stack (including Dovetail, Maze, and Rally), along with vendor relationships, budget, and build-versus-buy decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and improve Mercury’s AI-enabled workflows for research planning, customer conversations, and synthesis, maintaining high standards for evidence, privacy, and human judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pilot new ways of getting close to customers, such as rolling research programs and customer events like research dinners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make customer learning visible across Mercury, surfacing patterns that deepen teams’ understanding of the people they serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and coach one direct report, setting priorities and supporting their growth while staying hands on in the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of hands-on research operations experience and a track record of building or scaling a program with measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 1-2 years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a thought leader in the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have qualitative research experience and quantitative fluency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in ambiguity where the discipline isn&#39;t fully figured out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an excellent coach to non-researchers, building their judgment and confidence&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI in your daily work and stay curious about what&#39;s genuinely useful versus merely new&lt;/li&gt;
