&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers to define success, distinguish essential technical and domain expertise from skills that can be learned, and design thoughtful interview processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build targeted sourcing strategies for niche talent pools, including candidates whose backgrounds span data science, analytics, security, engineering, and financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic advisor to hiring leaders, using talent mapping, market insights, and recruiting data to inform hiring decisions and calibrate expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build lasting relationships with candidates and communicate a compelling, tailored story about their potential impact at Mercury.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion inclusive hiring practices and guide interview teams toward consistent, evidence-based decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead recruiting efforts for new and evolving roles, bringing structure to ambiguous searches and adapting your approach as you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use recruiting data to identify bottlenecks, strengthen pipelines, and improve hiring outcomes and candidate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flex across teams and role types as business priorities shift, bringing the same curiosity, urgency, and care to each search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 4+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience and 5+ years of overall experience in a talent, people, or HR-equivalent function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a track record of hiring for technical or quantitative roles in areas such as compliance analytics, data science, information security, or related functions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have direct experience recruiting for compliance and risk teams within fintech or financial services, with an understanding of how domain knowledge and regulatory requirements shape these searches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be comfortable learning technical concepts, discussing candidate backgrounds with specialized hiring teams, and translating complex requirements into effective sourcing and assessment strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be willing and able to take on engineering searches when needed, including information security engineering roles. Prior experience recruiting engineers is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience partnering with senior leaders and executives, influencing hiring decisions, and serving as a trusted advisor throughout a search.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring strong sourcing and networking skills, including the ability to build pipelines for specialized, emerging, or confidential hiring needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy creative problem solving, navigating ambiguity, and balancing competing priorities across different functions and role types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with empathy, kindness, and care, and enjoy building diverse, inclusive, and high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and precisely, with a strong sense of urgency and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
