&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As part of this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-impact, cross-functional, customer facing projects that touch Treasury engineering, operations, compliance, banking, and risk teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the technical architecture and experience of the Treasury product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, design, and operations to ship thoughtful features for our customers and internal users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and actively take responsibility for the product – we want someone excited to help shape and build Mercury’s future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a team of experienced and junior product engineers managing billions of dollars of customer assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The ideal candidate for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has 5+ years of professional full stack software engineering experience building and operating backend systems to customer facing experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicates and collaborates effectively with peers and cross-functional counterparts by being helpful and engaged&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a successful track record acting as the technical lead of complex projects with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a product-minded engineer who thinks about the developers consuming your APIs as well as always exceeding our customers expectations, not just shipping the feature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has domain knowledge of being a registered investment advisor and broker-dealer supporting both individual securities (equities, fixed income) as well as mutual funds&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to mentor both junior and senior engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
