&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is an in-office position, where you are expected to be in the office 5 days a week, from 9:00am - 5:00pm, with 2 days a month remote.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mercury is looking for a Workplace Experience Specialist to bring our culture to life in our New York office through the operations of daily life in the space. This role owns the day-to-day office experience for our NYC team, ensuring that the environment people walk into each day reflects Mercury&#39;s thoughtful approach to design, quality, and connection. Our offices are where teams build relationships, solve difficult problems together, and experience the culture that makes working here meaningful.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to running the daily experience, this role will support the cultural moments that punctuate the year: monthly office events, onsites hosted in NYC, and annual celebrations. You&#39;ll join a team that creates thoughtful, memorable moments for our employees with the same care we put into our products, and you&#39;ll partner closely with the broader People team, IT, and Finance on the larger operational pieces. Because our team is lean, your impact will be immediate — you&#39;ll set the tone for how Mercury&#39;s New York hub feels to the people in it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the on-site presence and cultural ambassador for the NYC office every day, welcoming employees, guests, candidates, and visiting teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the daily operations of the space — lunch, kitchen, supply stocking, incoming/outgoing mail and deliveries, and visitor management — acting as the first point of contact for office questions and requests, resolving what you can and escalating what needs a broader fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the office beautiful, organized, and aligned with Mercury’s aesthetic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape a distinct in-office culture by listening to employee feedback and thoughtfully balancing individual requests with team needs, resources, and the overall workplace experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own monthly office events from concept through execution, building a program of gatherings that reflects Mercury’s culture and draws the local team in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with onsite vendors (cleaning, catering, snacks, plants, building maintenance) and track facilities and building requests to resolution, operating within your office budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set up desks, meeting rooms, and AV for new hires, guests, and visiting teams, and own the basics of office access and safety (badges, visitor sign-in, emergency procedures).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the planning and execution of onsites and company events hosted in the NYC space, as well as broader employee experience initiatives — from All Hands and virtual events to merch production and cultural programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and lead improvements to office spaces, systems, and services to meet the evolving needs of a growing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate office updates, event invitations, and reminders clearly to the local team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to be in office M-F, 9:00am - 5:00pm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-3+ years of experience in office management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine warmth with people and an instinct for anticipating what someone needs before they ask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and the organization to keep a dozen small threads moving without dropping any.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment about what to solve yourself and what to escalate with a little guidance from your manager, and the initiative to act without waiting to be asked.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A refined eye for design and a deep appreciation for how a well-considered space makes people feel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, friendly written communication across Slack, email, and signage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative team player who proactively asks for and acts on feedback, and pitches in on team activities beyond your core responsibilities when the opportunity comes up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;NYC-based, with the expectation that you’re in the office every day — this role is on-site and hands-on by design, including moving boxes, resetting furniture, and being on your feet. Ability to lift 25 pounds if needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about people and what makes a space feel special.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
